  "summary": "Migration adds inventory stock movement metadata/cost fields and stock item configuration, plus packaging/prep recipe tables with restrictive references and a cascading PrepRecipeLines->PrepRecipes relation; source indices support those references. Existing InventoryItems/StockMovements rows are extended without backfill: Direction is nonnull with default \"\" (and new items get false/empty/zero defaults). Current readers compare Direction with StockDirection.In and one mapper uses Enum.Parse; if pre-existing stock movement rows exist, blank values may be treated as outbound in sign-based balances or fail parsing. This is a conditional data-transition risk, not proof that deployed rows exist or are affected. No canonical promotion without data-history/current-model corroboration.",
